    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73620",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $5$th columns.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
