  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-77487",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row",
      "problem": "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{21}+5\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-0)+5(-6-4) \\\\  & =3-50 \\\\  & =-47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+5\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-2)-5(-8-4) \\\\  & =-2+60 \\\\  & =58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-47+58=11.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-12",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-52",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "11",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "21",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "25",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
