      "knowledge_point_id": "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column",
      "problem": "$|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{14}+2\\cdot {C}_{24}+0\\cdot {C}_{34}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
