      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column",
      "problem": "$|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using a cofactor expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot {C}_{43} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-1)^{4+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
