  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081590",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-158371",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3118d2af-771f-54c9-b18e-5196b87b6dca",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Volume of an N-Dimensional Parallelepiped",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $1$st row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8(-14+30) \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|128|=128.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
